From ad37071ae6bbc4a31289f9e662388c50e92ac3d3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Costa Xanthos <constantinexanthos@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 19:56:50 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Fix inflated realized P&L: stop recording unfilled legs as
 positions
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

record_fill created a Trade + Position for every leg in the signal even
when execution_results only covered the legs that actually filled. In a
cross-platform arb where Polymarket filled and Kalshi failed (or vice
versa), the unfilled leg became a phantom position at the requested size.
At settlement it was closed as if it had been bought, booking the arb's
"guaranteed" edge (or a fake win) that never happened on the exchange.

Two related matching bugs made this worse:
- Polymarket (py-clob-client) results carry no ticker, so the positional
  fallback could apply a Kalshi order's fill_count/price to a Poly leg.
- Polymarket order IDs use orderID (camel case) and were dropped, so
  those trades had no order_id even when they really filled.

Changes:
- record_fill: in live mode, only record legs with a matching execution
  result (ticker + venue). No positional fallback. Read orderID too.
- event_loop: tag every Kalshi/Polymarket result with ticker and venue.
- _upsert_position / get_open_position: never merge a paper fill into a
  live position (or vice versa) — match on is_paper as well.
- scripts/sql/audit_phantom_positions.sql: find closed live positions
  with no exchange order_id and quantify their P&L; repair is opt-in.
- tests/test_portfolio_manager.py: regression coverage.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
